              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LaniQ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good. I forgot to use the mustard, but the crunch of the walnuts was wonderful. I also did not have fresh dill, so I used 1-1 1/2 Tb. dried. My 4 kids LOVED it and all had seconds."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Janis M Krauss-krieger"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used two full salmon filet, skinned and portioned before baking. I thought the dill sounded strange with the walnuts so I omitted it. Six tablespoons of zest is a bit much. I used 1 Tbsp zest (3 lemons) and 2 tsp lemon pepper. Added 2 Tbsp of dark brown sugar. Grill the lemons for sweetness and squeeze over top at the end. This recipe made twice as much topping as I needed, but that is OK. I will freeze it for another time. Cold leftovers great over kale salad.",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-20T22:35:55.203Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My wife and I really enjoyed this, but I made a few modifications: I didn't have lemons, so no lemon juice or lemon rinds. I used lemon pepper seasoning, black &amp; cayenne pepper, onion &amp; garlic powder in the walnut crust mix (maybe 1 tsp each). I also seasoned the salmon filets with salt, pepper, store-bought italian seasoning and diced yellow onions and let it all marinate for about 20 mins. After baking for 20 minutes, I set the oven to broil for 2-3 minutes (watch carefully- crumbs will blacken). I will definitely use this recipe again to impress some house guests.",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-28T18:26:17.100Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
